I do my very best to capture the image properly in-camera. I have a thing for level images with strong composition and framing, and try to find elements that will complement the image instead of being a distraction. I prefer to shoot with prime lenses but appreciate the versatility of zooms when necessary.

My editing tends toward a cinematic tone with cooler undertones and muted greens without compromising skin tones or making the scene and subject look unrealistic. While I enjoy the nostalgia of shooting on film and want to nod towards that style, I don't shoot on film so I'm not going to try and pretend that I do. I want my images to look and feel timeless.
